NAME
       losetup - set up and list loop devices (a file used as a disk)

SYNOPSIS
       losetup [-a]
       losetup -f --show FILE
       losetup -d LOOPDEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       A loop device (/dev/loop0, /dev/loop1...) makes a regular file look
       like a block device, so you can partition it, make a file system on
       it, or mount a disk image. mount -o loop FILE DIR sets one up for you.

OPTIONS
       -a, --all
              List the loop devices in use and their files (also the default
              without arguments).

       -f, --find
              Use the first free loop device. With --show, print its name.

       -d     Detach a loop device from its file.

EXAMPLES
           losetup -a

NOTES
       Cert Lab does not simulate loop devices: only the listing works. Use
       the spare disks /dev/vdb and /dev/vdc for practice instead.

SEE ALSO
       mount(8), lsblk(8)
